btd TODO
========

Security
--------

- engine_adv_report: match the address type, not only the bytes.
- avdtp.c: a peer OPEN while streaming moves to A2DP_S_PEER: a2dp_stop
  does nothing and rtp_frame uses the freed rtp.chan.  Key a2dp_stop on
  rtp.chan, reject OPEN unless configured.
- avdtp_accept, avctp_accept: channels accepted before sig/media/chan is
  set keep arg on freed memory after a2dp_down/avrcp_down.
- device_reconf during an SDP query frees the device; sdpc_close then
  calls a2dp_sdp with the stale q->dev.
- L2CAP before authentication: limit channels per connection, time out
  a channel that never gets CONFIG_REQ, keep next_cid off CIDs in use,
  bound aclq.  l2cap_disconn_req: check the source CID against ch->rcid.
- hogp_chars, hogp_descs, hogp_bat_chars: require last >= start, a peer
  can loop discovery.
- -vvv logs LTKs, link keys, SMP keys and HID reports (keystrokes).
  Redact key-bearing packets, drop ACL payloads, clamp the verbosity the
  control socket accepts.
- bus: root, no pledge, forwards any HCI opcode and wscons event type.
  Allow key events to wskbd, mouse events to wsmouse and a list of HCI
  opcodes; consider holding the device fds and dropping to _btd,
  RLIMIT_NPROC 0 after the reader fork.  Document the trust boundary in
  btd.8.
- SMP: compare only X when rejecting a reflected public key; reject the
  SC debug public key and the BR debug link key (type 3); validate the
  IO capability and reserved bits of the pairing response.
- Key material: freezero the hci.c command structs carrying an LTK or
  link key; explicit_bzero the bus buffer, cmac() mb/ob, main's stack
  bond copy and bond_read's line buffer; BN_clear_free the DH secret.
- Bonds file: check owner and mode, fsync the directory after the
  rename, parse strictly (%2x takes 0x, strtoull takes a minus sign),
  a bad local line half-overwrites the identity, duplicates are kept.
- Privsep: main validates bond type/keysize and caps the count; struct
  bond and hid_conf send TAILQ pointers over imsg; a duplicate
  IMSG_DEVFD_* leaks the old fd; drop sendfd in main and recvfd in
  frontend after startup; check daemon(); O_CLOEXEC on the lock fd.
- Control socket: getpeereid, root only for reload, log and unpair;
  reject a payload on SHOW; replies are routed by the pid the client
  sets.
- sndio: a missing or badly permissioned cookie makes libsndio mkdir()
  and abort the frontend pledge.  Check it first, or open sndio only
  with a headset configured.
- sbc_init: cap bitpool at 250, above it the frame overflows audio.c
  frame[512]; check the length.
- Hostile controller: ACL past the 4100 byte buffer is dropped silently
  and desyncs the stream; reject a duplicate connection handle; acl_num
  0 grows aclq forever.

Bugs
----

- sdp_send writes the fragment length as continuation state, the caller
  reads an offset: responses of 3 or more fragments repeat or skip data.
  Pass cont in and write cont + n.
- a2dp_parse_config ignores rate and bitpool from btd.conf when the
  headset sends SET_CONFIGURATION.  Fix or document.
- "headset X { }" is a syntax error: headsetopts_l needs an option.
- btd.c: a SIGHUP reload logs at debug, a btctl reload at info.
- A link refused for its security (key size, E0 with a Secure
  Connections key, authentication failure) is retried every
  DEV_HEADSET_RETRY seconds forever.  Back off, or wait for a reload or
  "btctl unpair".

Daemon conventions
------------------

- daemon(1, 0): with a relative -f the unveil and reload use /.
- log_init runs before the device opens: startup errors go to syslog
  only.  Move it right before daemon().
- main_reload ignores send errors; return them and keep the old config.
- btd.c: missing break after main_shutdown in the signal handler;
  main_sendall declared, not defined; imsgbuf_flush results ignored in
  main_imsg_send_ipc_sockets; verbosity set before parse_config.
- parse.y: log_getverbose() == 1 / == 2 should be >=; check_file_secrecy
  is dead code; /*empty*/ -> /* empty */.
- frontend: imsgbuf_write before imsgbuf_clear at shutdown.
- btctl: no "log debug" level, -vvv unreachable at runtime.
- style(9): 28 lines over 80 columns; module-local functions not
  static; I2S macro return without parentheses; control.c include
  order.
- log.c, log.h: drop the copied $OpenBSD$ IDs and the unused SMALL
  block.
- regress: NOMAN is redundant; add a parse regress with -nv golden
  files; crypto: f4 with z 0x80/0x81, a known P-256 key pair, X-only
  reflection, debug key.

Documentation
-------------

- btd.8:
  - only 2357:0604 is known, other RTL8761BU need "firmware".
  - document SIGHUP, and that device and firmware need a restart.
  - keyboard LEDs and /dev/wskbd0, /dev/btd.lock in FILES.
  - the engine pledges "stdio recvfd", not "stdio".
  - the sndiod sub-device must be named mon; "the SBC rate" is the
    configured rate.
  - PAIRING and AUDIO as .Ss, HOTPLUG under EXAMPLES; add STANDARDS
    (Core, HOGP, BAS, A2DP, AVDTP, AVRCP, RFC 3550), AUTHORS.
  - SEE ALSO sndioctl 1, hotplugd 8; only usb0 to usb9 are scanned;
    LE legacy pairing is refused; the local name is the hostname.
- btd.conf.5: firmware is Realtek only; add a macro example and a lead-in
  before the keywords; colon-separated, two digits per octet; .Cm for
  the rates; describe the FILES entry; mention the audio role.
- btctl.8: "log verbose" is level 2 (-vv).
- Comments: hci_cmd_noreply should say msec holds the queue; rtp_frame
  misses the RTP_MAX_FRAMES flush and MTU drop; btd.h "/* engine */"
  covers shared constants; bond.c format omits blank and # lines;
  bus.c "X" -> "the X server"; hid_test "hand made" -> "hand-made".
- README: give the dropped-audio paragraph its own heading;
  "privilege-separated"; the SBC regress is skipped without ffmpeg.
- Changes: 0.1 is unreleased but lists fixes to earlier behaviour.
